From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: dts: ingenic: marmot: drop the duplicate ext clock

Commit 0124 renamed the oscillator node in both t41.dtsi and marmot.dts
to /ext but kept the extclk label on both.  DTC aborts the marmot build
with a duplicate_label error:

  marmot.dts:219.17-221.4: ERROR (duplicate_label): /extclk:
  Duplicate label 'extclk' on /extclk and /ext

The SoC tree already describes the 24 MHz oscillator, so the board copy
is redundant.  Remove it and let the label from t41.dtsi stand.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/marmot.dts
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/marmot.dts
@@ -216,10 +216,6 @@
 
 / {
 
-	extclk: ext {
-		clock-frequency = <24000000>;
-	};
-
 	gpio_keys: gpio_keys {
 		compatible = "gpio-keys";
 
